%N A086350 Square array of Pell related numbers, read by antidiagonals.
%C A086350 Rows are successive binomial transforms of (1, 1, 2, 2, 4, 4, ...).
%C A086350 T(n,c) can be created applying the pos operator (which sums over the positive coefficients) to the n-th power of the Floretion element 'ki' - 'kj' + c*'ee', c>=0. This follows from ('ki' - 'kj')^2 = 2'ee'. - _Meghanto Majumder_, Oct 02 2026
%F A086350 T(n, k) = ((1+sqrt(2)) * (k+sqrt(2))^n - (1-sqrt(2)) * (k-sqrt(2))^n) / sqrt(8).
